{
  "about": "Realtime engine scenarios every AgentChat SDK runs against its own RealtimeClient: a mock socket, a fake REST client and one recording message.new handler. Each scenario runs twice, once per mode: 'default' (ack after every handler finished) and 'ack_on_receipt'. The REST client serves sync_pages in order, then empty pages; sync/ack records the cursor; gap-fill returns nothing. The automatic drain on hello.ok is off and reconnect is off, so only the steps below act. A message is 'handled' when its handler finished without raising; a sync/ack cursor 'covers' every row served so far up to and including the row carrying that delivery_id. Results are read after the last step and any started drain finished, before the client is disconnected (disconnect flushes parked frames).",
  "expectations": {
    "cursor_acks": "Exactly these delivery_ids were passed to sync/ack, in order.",
    "dispatched": "Exactly these message ids reached the handler, in this order.",
    "dispatched_includes": "These message ids reached the handler (others may too).",
    "ws_acks": "Exactly these message ids were sent in ack frames, in order."
  },
  "invariants": {
    "acked_was_handled": "At the end, every message the client acknowledged (an ack frame, or a row a sync/ack cursor covers) was handled. An ack is a promise the server never re-offers the message.",
    "acks_follow_handling": "When each sync/ack cursor is sent (both modes), and each ack frame in the default mode, every message it acknowledges was already handled. Under ack_on_receipt an ack frame is sent at receipt, before the handler.",
    "dispatched_once": "No message id reaches the handler twice in these scenarios.",
    "seq_order": "Within one conversation the handler sees seqs in ascending order.",
    "serial_per_conversation": "Within one conversation the handler is never entered for a message while it is still running for another one: one message at a time, in seq order. Different conversations run concurrently."
  },
  "ops": {
    "close": "The server side ends the socket with close code 1006 (an abnormal drop).",
    "connect": "Create the client for the mode, connect, open the socket and answer HELLO with {\"type\": \"hello.ok\", \"capabilities\": [\"ack\"]}.",
    "drain": "Start the client's offline drain (drainOfflineEnvelopes / drain_offline_envelopes) without awaiting it.",
    "frame": "The server sends {\"type\": \"message.new\", \"payload\": <payload>} on the socket.",
    "gap_window_lapses": "Wait until the 2 s gap window has passed, so the client resolves the open gap (the REST gap fill returns nothing) and hands the parked frames over.",
    "reconnect": "After a close, connect the same client again: a new socket opens and HELLO is answered as in connect. The client's dedup cache and the dispatches still running carry over; the ordering state does not.",
    "release": "Let the held handler for message_id finish.",
    "wait_handler": "Wait until the handler has been entered for message_id."
  },
  "rules": "Every op is followed by letting the client run until it is idle (pending handlers that are held stay pending). The handler blocks on the ids in 'hold' until a 'release' step, and raises for the ids in 'fail'. A harness rejects an op, expectation or invariant name it does not implement. A scenario with \"no_handler\": true registers no message.new handler at all.",
